<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rugila</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died c. 435</span> · Also known as Rua, Ruga</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rugila, also called Rua, was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huns">Huns</a> in the 420s and 430s and the uncle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attila">Attila</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bleda">Bleda</a>. He concentrated power among the Huns of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> plain, received tribute from the Eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> and supported the Roman general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flavius-aetius">Aetius</a> in the West. On his death around 435 his nephews succeeded him.</p></div>
